---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="xnoto.dev — platform infrastructure and agentic operations"
  description="Personal portfolio and field notes on platform infrastructure, developer workflows, and agentic operations."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Personal systems notebook</p>
      <h1>Platforms, tools, and the humans who have to operate them.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I work on platform infrastructure, developer workflows, and the systems around AI agents.
        This is a place for source-backed projects, design notes, and the lessons that survive contact with real constraints.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="profile-link" href="https://github.com/xnoto" aria-label="Steven Welch on GitHub">
      <img
        class="profile-image"
        src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121333299?v=4"
        alt="Steven Welch"
        width="400"
        height="400"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </a>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="start-here">
    <h2 id="start-here">Start here</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="status">Architecture</p>
        <h3><a href="/agentic-platform-operations/">Agentic platform operations</a></h3>
        <p>How tool-scoped agents, validation, evidence, and human approval fit together.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="status">Source-backed</p>
        <h3><a href="/projects/">Projects</a></h3>
        <p>A small catalog of maintained work, reference designs, and archived experiments.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="status">Operations lab</p>
        <h3><a href="https://makeitwork.cloud">Make IT Work</a></h3>
        <p>A separate personal DevOps portal for operational services and infrastructure exploration.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="working-style">
    <h2 id="working-style">Working style</h2>
    <p>
      The useful part of an agentic workflow is not that it looks autonomous. It is that its tools,
      boundaries, validation, and resulting evidence are clear enough for a person to review and trust.
    </p>
    <p>
      Project pages here distinguish what public source demonstrates from what is a reference design,
      experiment, or future direction. That distinction is part of the work.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
